From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marvin Scholz <epirat07@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:22:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libavformat/flvdec: validate avio_read size on extended data

Use ffio_read_size in flv_parse_mod_ex_data to ensure that an error is returned
if the complete ex_size chunk wasn't read, instead of reading uninitialized data.

This fixes a MemorySanitizer use-of-uninitialized-value issue where a short read
would leave the buffer partially uninitialized before parsing nano_offset.

Signed-off-by: Marvin Scholz <epirat07@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5385979defeac64931213559de8a04ff0a750b2c)
---
 libavformat/flvdec.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/flvdec.c b/libavformat/flvdec.c
index 0331050..f480cd3 100644
--- a/libavformat/flvdec.c
+++ b/libavformat/flvdec.c
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 #include "libavutil/intreadwrite.h"
 #include "libavutil/mastering_display_metadata.h"
 #include "avformat.h"
+#include "avio_internal.h"
 #include "demux.h"
 #include "internal.h"
 #include "flv.h"
@@ -1342,7 +1343,7 @@ static int flv_parse_mod_ex_data(AVFormatContext *s, int *pkt_type, int *size, i
     if (!ex_data)
         return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
 
-    ret = avio_read(s->pb, ex_data, ex_size);
+    ret = ffio_read_size(s->pb, ex_data, ex_size);
     if (ret < 0) {
         av_free(ex_data);
         return ret;
